WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.533
 Ready for this?

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.135
 Oh, yes, sir.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.146
NARRATOR: General
George Washington's

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.647
lion-headed cuttoe.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:20.119
One of only two swords worn
by General George Washington

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.755
during the Revolutionary
War, the lion-headed cuttoe

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:24.490
was Washington's
trusted side arm

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.160
during early
American engagements.

00:00:27.227 --> 00:00:28.561
He was proud that
the weapon was made

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.963
in America, having been
custom forged by a bladesmith

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.598
in Philadelphia.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.800
Lethal in battle, the
sword was designed

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:36.669
for rapid cuts
and brutal thrusts

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:38.271
to take down an opponent.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.339
In the famous painting,
"Washington Crossing

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.876
the Delaware",
artist Emanuel Leutze

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.710
places a more refined
weapon at the General's

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:48.181
left side, which he did not
acquire until several years

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.315
later.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:51.383
In reality, the sword
carried by Washington

00:00:51.483 --> 00:00:56.488
on that fateful crossing was
likely his lion-headed cuttoe.

00:00:56.589 --> 00:01:01.161
 All right, veterans,
welcome to the kill test.

00:01:01.227 --> 00:01:03.897
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.565
I will take your weapon
and deliver killing

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.633
blows to this pig carcass.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.467
Tyler, you're up first.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:09.568
Ready?

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:11.704
[laughter]

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.539
 I'm ready.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:38.931
 All right, Tyler, your
handle construction just right.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:42.168
Your edge is very sharp.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:45.805
Overall, sir, this
saber will kill.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.907
 Perfect.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.042
 All right, Gene,
your turn, sir.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.909
You ready?

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:50.643
 Let's do this, Doug.

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:18.938
 All right, Gene.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.207
This is a heavy sword,
very forward heavy.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.509
But when you have a forward
heavy blade that you're hitting

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:27.513
and it meets resistance,
a cylindrical, almost

00:02:27.579 --> 00:02:31.250
circular handle makes
it twist in my hand.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.720
So probably, there is a
reason why the chain came off.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.856
But your blade is sharp.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:37.790
It will kill.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.196
All right, gentlemen.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.966
December 25th, 1776,
George Washington

00:02:47.066 --> 00:02:50.302
leads the Continental Army
across a frozen Delaware River

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.905
to attack the Hessians
at Trenton, New Jersey.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.740
And he probably didn't chip
his way through the ice.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:57.277
But that's not going to keep
us from our strength test,

00:02:57.377 --> 00:03:00.112
the ice block chop.

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:00.979
Tyler, you're up first.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.248
Are you ready?

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.383
 Yeah, let's do it.

00:03:25.637 --> 00:03:28.007
 All right, so Tyler,
your chain fell off.

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:30.710
But there's no
damage on your edge.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.945
Your handle's comfortable.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.746
Other than the
chain, you nailed it.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.281
Good job.

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.349
All right, Gene.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:36.983
 Do it.

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:05.178
 All right, Gene.

00:04:05.245 --> 00:04:08.614
Your blade's edge is still
there and still sharp.

00:04:08.681 --> 00:04:11.884
The issue is the rest
of your chain fell off

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.452
and it's picked up a bent.

00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:16.756
I have less issue with
that and more issue

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.257
with this polished handle.

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:21.327
It's just hard to hold on to.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:26.232
It is strong and it does
have an edge, so good job.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:28.134
 [inaudible] .

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.469
 All right, veterans,
our sharpest test today

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.005
is the Hessian charge.

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:37.109
This is all about what your
edge will do to these dummies.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:37.943
Tyler, you're up first.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:38.710
You ready for this?

00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:39.612
 Yeah.

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.242
 All right, Tyler, the
weight of your weapon

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.278
does prevent me from
going very fast.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.547
But you have a very sharp
edge all the way through.

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:16.715
Your weapon, sir, it will cut.

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.216
 Thank you.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.385
 All right, Gene,
it's your turn.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:20.285
Are you ready?

00:05:20.352 --> 00:05:20.987
 Let's do this, Doug.

00:05:50.782 --> 00:05:54.286
 All right, Gene, to be able
to maintain a good grip on this,

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:55.688
more of the cuts
I create are more

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:58.156
impact as opposed
to a slash where

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.524
it cuts all the way through.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.093
So we have some
cuts here that are

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:05.364
more nicks, deep nicks because
you have a very sharp edge.

00:06:05.431 --> 00:06:09.134
And for this test, sir,
your weapon will cut.

00:06:09.201 --> 00:06:12.338
 Awesome.

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:15.108
 It takes a lot of guts to
get out there and compete.

00:06:15.174 --> 00:06:16.275
I'm glad I did it.

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.577
And to come this far
is pretty amazing.

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.346 line:8%
 I've definitely
got the competition

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:21.714 line:14%
that I was expecting from Gene.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.416
But I think it's
going to come down

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:26.886
to the wire between the both
of us at the end of this.

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.855
 Tyler, Gene, first
of all, I want to thank

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.355
you both for your service.

00:06:30.422 --> 00:06:32.158
You're both
champions in my mind.

00:06:32.258 --> 00:06:35.060
You've already won
your branch divisions.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.364
But there can only be one
Battle of the Branches champion

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:43.035
when you walk out of here
with a check for $50,000.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:48.207
And that champion is Tyler.

00:06:48.274 --> 00:06:49.441
Congratulations.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:51.343
You are the Battle
of the Branches

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:53.378
Forged in Fire champion.

00:06:53.445 --> 00:06:57.049
Gene, your blade
didn't make the cut.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:07:00.286
Please surrender your blade.

00:07:00.352 --> 00:07:01.787
 There's a lot of
Marines out there.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.622
And there's a lot of great
guys in the Marine Corps.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.257
And so for me to stand
here and represent

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:06.992
them is pretty humbling.

00:07:07.059 --> 00:07:08.361
 Tyler, congratulations.

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:11.630
You overcame every obstacle
set in front of you.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.632
You beat out all
the other smiths.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.534
And now you're the
Battle of the Branches

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.102
Forged in Fire champion.

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:22.274
That's a title that comes with
a check for $50,000 and, most

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:24.543
importantly, bragging rights.

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.877
Good job, my brother.

00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:29.549
Please present your
blade to the judges.

00:07:29.649 --> 00:07:31.384
 I'm super excited.

00:07:31.451 --> 00:07:33.452
When this whole thing
started, I had no idea how

00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:34.920
it was all going to turn out.

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.689
Feels good to have
represented the Army.

00:07:37.789 --> 00:07:43.662
The fact that I just won
$50,000 is starting to set in.

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:46.966
I'm Sergeant Tyler Hackbarth
and I'm the new Battle

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:48.000
of the Branches champion.

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:02.414
 George Washington's
colichemarde.

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:03.682
I've never even
heard of this thing.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:04.817 line:14%
Never seen it, nothing.

00:08:04.917 --> 00:08:06.251 line:8%
Right now, my heart
is just racing,

00:08:06.318 --> 00:08:07.820
because I'm freaking out.

00:08:07.886 --> 00:08:09.888
NARRATOR: The colichemarde was
a unique dueling sword that

00:08:09.955 --> 00:08:12.691
became popular during
the late 17th century

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:15.527
and was a favorite blade
style of George Washington.

00:08:15.628 --> 00:08:17.163
The weapon had an
extremely broad

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:20.566
forte, [inaudible] skate
blade ample parrying strength.

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:23.735
However, the sword rapidly
tapered to a big point,

00:08:23.835 --> 00:08:26.805
allowing for precise thrusting
and stabbing attacks.

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:29.408
An avid sword collector,
George Washington

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:32.011
even had a colichemarde
blade small sword

00:08:32.111 --> 00:08:34.880
at his side while swearing in
as America's first president.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:38.617
The weapon was such an iconic
part of Washington's persona,

00:08:38.717 --> 00:08:40.986
it can even be spotted
alongside the first president

00:08:41.086 --> 00:08:44.990
in this iconic 1824
John Trumbull painting.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:46.992
 To find out what
kind of lethal damage

00:08:47.092 --> 00:08:49.462
your weapon will do, I
will take your colichemarde

00:08:49.562 --> 00:08:52.731
for harassing cuts and
thrust to this pig carcass.

00:08:52.798 --> 00:08:53.499
Josh, you're up first.

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:54.433
Are you ready?

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.301
 Not really, but go ahead.

00:09:21.259 --> 00:09:24.196
 All right, Josh, first up,
it's got a nice weight to it.

00:09:24.262 --> 00:09:28.200
Now your handle construction,
it is small enough to where

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.501
I can get my hand around it.

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:30.836
But it doesn't roll.

00:09:30.902 --> 00:09:34.874
Your edge, as you
can see, is sharp.

00:09:34.941 --> 00:09:35.841
It will kill.

00:09:35.942 --> 00:09:36.808
 Thank you, sir.

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.277
 All right, Dan.
It's your turn.

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:38.977
You ready for this?

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:39.912
 Let's do it.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:18.184
 All right, Dan, you have
a very aggressive tip.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.786
The thrusting worked very well.

00:10:20.853 --> 00:10:23.922
But your edges right
here are not sharp.

00:10:24.022 --> 00:10:26.425
I can even move it
around with my glove.

00:10:26.492 --> 00:10:27.692
It's not cutting it.

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:30.962
You can see that your
blade took a bend.

00:10:31.062 --> 00:10:33.398
But overall, because
you're able to thrust,

00:10:33.465 --> 00:10:35.267
this blade, sir, will kill.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:36.102
 Thank you.

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:41.974
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test,

00:10:42.074 --> 00:10:46.145
our cherrywood chop in
honor of George Washington.

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:49.814
The colichemarde was known as
a fast, light, flexible weapon.

00:10:49.914 --> 00:10:51.517
It was designed for the duel.

00:10:51.583 --> 00:10:53.686
So to test the
strength of your blade,

00:10:53.753 --> 00:10:56.288
I'll be doing several tip
cuts against that wood

00:10:56.389 --> 00:10:57.822
and then thrusting
into it, flexing

00:10:57.922 --> 00:10:59.358
your blade in both directions.

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:01.593
Make sure that tempers
right and that that blade

00:11:01.693 --> 00:11:02.861
doesn't pick up a set.

00:11:02.961 --> 00:11:04.296
Josh, you're up first.
You're ready?

00:11:04.396 --> 00:11:05.197
 Go for it.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:36.562
 All right, Josh.

00:11:36.629 --> 00:11:38.597
There are a lot of
pointy bits on this guard

00:11:38.697 --> 00:11:39.865
that don't need to be there.

00:11:39.965 --> 00:11:43.001
That really digs
right into your hand.

00:11:43.102 --> 00:11:46.271
Other than that, did well
and flexed very nicely

00:11:46.338 --> 00:11:47.639
and came back to true.

00:11:47.706 --> 00:11:48.373
So good job.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:49.941
 Thank you.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:51.777
 All right, Dan,
are you ready to go?

00:11:51.844 --> 00:11:53.112
 Sure, let's go.

00:12:17.102 --> 00:12:19.838
 I commend your effort
in making a blade

00:12:19.905 --> 00:12:22.173
that's very nicely done.

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:26.345
But the heat treat on this
blade has just failed.

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:32.951
I no longer know where the tip
it, which is disappointing,

00:12:33.018 --> 00:12:34.786
because I think you
did a beautiful job

00:12:34.853 --> 00:12:36.122
constructing this weapon.

00:12:40.158 --> 00:12:43.395
 All right, bladesmiths, to
find out how sharp your weapons

00:12:43.462 --> 00:12:46.398
are, I will take a colichemarde
and deliver harassing slashes

00:12:46.498 --> 00:12:48.734
and thrust on these sandbags.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.335
Josh, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:12:50.402 --> 00:12:51.137
 Sure.

00:13:30.875 --> 00:13:32.244
 All right, Josh.

00:13:32.311 --> 00:13:35.180
Once again, very sharp edge
on your blade right here.

00:13:35.247 --> 00:13:37.615
Easily cuts through
these sandbags.

00:13:37.716 --> 00:13:38.950
It stayed true.

00:13:39.017 --> 00:13:42.353
Easy to align and see
my target and cut it.

00:13:42.454 --> 00:13:43.855
And it will cut.

00:13:43.922 --> 00:13:45.291
 Thank you.

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:46.391
 Dan, you're ready?

00:13:46.458 --> 00:13:47.259
 Yep.

00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:48.093
 Let's do this.

00:14:04.376 --> 00:14:07.879
Dan, when I look at the
bend on this colichemarde,

00:14:07.979 --> 00:14:10.115
I won't be able to
stab straight and true.

00:14:10.215 --> 00:14:12.050
I won't really know
where the tip is.

00:14:12.117 --> 00:14:14.286
And for me, that's
a real problem.

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:17.021
I don't feel like I can test
this blade in the same way

00:14:17.121 --> 00:14:18.857
I can test the blade before it.

00:14:18.924 --> 00:14:20.959
Because if I have to do
any kind of corrections,

00:14:21.026 --> 00:14:24.029
that's not a fair test.

00:14:24.096 --> 00:14:27.666
 Unfortunately, Dan, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:14:27.733 --> 00:14:28.834
And for that reason,
I have to ask

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.103
you to please leave the forge.

00:14:31.203 --> 00:14:35.340
 As a period piece, as a wall
hanger, my blade was spot on.

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.509
But as a sword, it just
didn't make the cut.

00:14:37.576 --> 00:14:39.978
 Josh, you are the new
Forged in Fire champion.

00:14:40.078 --> 00:14:44.783
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.418
Good job.

00:14:46.485 --> 00:14:49.788
 This is hands down one of
the best moments of my life.

00:14:49.855 --> 00:14:51.390
 Good job.

00:14:51.457 --> 00:14:54.092
 To my wife and my kids, this
just proves that you can do it.

00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:55.627
It's just a matter
putting your mind to it

00:14:55.727 --> 00:14:56.562
and putting your heart in.

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:09.441
 Ulysses Grant's
Donaldson sword.

00:15:11.777 --> 00:15:14.279
NARRATOR: The Donaldson sword
is a commemorative blade awarded

00:15:14.346 --> 00:15:16.915
to General Ulysses S.
Grant for his victory

00:15:16.982 --> 00:15:20.251
at Fort Donaldson
in February of 1862,

00:15:20.318 --> 00:15:23.622
one of the first major union
victories of the Civil War.

00:15:23.689 --> 00:15:25.257
The weapon features
a highly ornate

00:15:25.323 --> 00:15:29.227
handle an engraved blade based
on the popular 1862 officer

00:15:29.294 --> 00:15:30.595
sword.

00:15:30.662 --> 00:15:32.964
After General Grant's death,
his wife donated the sword

00:15:33.064 --> 00:15:35.768
to the Smithsonian
Institute in 1886

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:39.404
and it remains under
their care to this day.

00:15:39.471 --> 00:15:42.241
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:15:42.308 --> 00:15:45.176
The sword was made to be
a dueling type of weapon.

00:15:45.276 --> 00:15:48.080
So I'm going to try to
deliver the same light slashes

00:15:48.146 --> 00:15:50.582
and thrust on this
ballistics dummy.

00:15:50.649 --> 00:15:51.749
Paul, you ready for this?

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:52.717
 Oh, yes, sir.

00:15:52.784 --> 00:15:54.019
 All right, let's do this.

00:16:17.542 --> 00:16:19.544
All right, Paul. let's talk
about your version of General

00:16:19.611 --> 00:16:21.179
Grant's Donaldson sword.

00:16:21.246 --> 00:16:26.085
The weight on this blade is
not that of a dueling sword,

00:16:26.185 --> 00:16:30.622
because it requires a little bit
more than just wrist movement.

00:16:30.722 --> 00:16:32.824
But it is a great cutting sword.

00:16:32.891 --> 00:16:35.160
Your edges are sharp.

00:16:35.227 --> 00:16:36.828
Even with the harassing
cut, you can see,

00:16:36.895 --> 00:16:38.163
they're cutting deeply.

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:42.801
And more importantly,
sir, it will kill.

00:16:42.868 --> 00:16:43.702
Isaac, your turn, sir.

00:16:43.802 --> 00:16:44.502
You ready for this?

00:16:44.569 --> 00:16:45.370
 I guess.

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:46.205
 OK.

00:17:05.590 --> 00:17:08.059
All right, Isaac, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:17:08.159 --> 00:17:09.695
What I like about
it is the time you

00:17:09.762 --> 00:17:12.130
took to put these
details that we

00:17:12.196 --> 00:17:14.867
were asking for on your sword.

00:17:14.933 --> 00:17:18.603
Every cut was deep and
not a lot of powers

00:17:18.704 --> 00:17:21.206
required when you're
swinging something so light.

00:17:21.273 --> 00:17:24.976
But probably hitting
the bone, your blade

00:17:25.043 --> 00:17:28.479
did take a slight bend.

00:17:28.546 --> 00:17:32.450
But overall, sir,
your weapon will kill.

00:17:32.517 --> 00:17:33.252
 Thank you.

00:17:36.922 --> 00:17:38.857
 Paul, Isaac, you
know what time it is,

00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:40.792
time for the strength
test, a fan favorite

00:17:40.892 --> 00:17:44.496
and the cringeworthy flex test.

00:17:44.596 --> 00:17:46.831
And we're going to
flex those blades to 35

00:17:46.898 --> 00:17:48.299
degrees in either direction.

00:17:48.399 --> 00:17:50.268
If you're still holding
true, we're going to go to 45

00:17:50.335 --> 00:17:52.837
degrees in either direction.

00:17:52.904 --> 00:17:54.138
Paul, you ready for this?

00:17:54.205 --> 00:17:56.475
 Not really, but go
ahead and bend away.

00:18:33.745 --> 00:18:36.815
 So Paul, as far as the
construction of your blade

00:18:36.881 --> 00:18:38.216
goes, the handle's comfortable.

00:18:38.282 --> 00:18:40.652
We saw how well this sword cuts.

00:18:40.719 --> 00:18:41.820
You did a good job.

00:18:41.887 --> 00:18:44.256
But if you look
into that blade, you

00:18:44.356 --> 00:18:48.093
can actually see a dark spot
on both sides of this blade.

00:18:48.159 --> 00:18:50.996
And whether that's a
flaw that you picked up

00:18:51.063 --> 00:18:54.165
in the forging process
or a flaw in the steel,

00:18:54.265 --> 00:18:56.234
I have no way of really
telling right now.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.236
But the grain structure
on this looks fine.

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:01.273
But having it shatter,
having it pop like that,

00:19:01.373 --> 00:19:02.341
that's a big issue.

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:10.348
 Well, Paul, we absolutely
hate to see that.

00:19:10.448 --> 00:19:12.284
You put a lot of
work into your blade.

00:19:12.384 --> 00:19:15.153
You made it past the
35 on both sides,

00:19:15.219 --> 00:19:17.222
but you did break
on the way to 45.

00:19:17.322 --> 00:19:18.756
But you're not out
of the fight yet.

00:19:18.823 --> 00:19:21.793
Isaac, you've got to survive
both of the 35 degree turns

00:19:21.893 --> 00:19:26.464
as well as the official ruling
of 40 degrees toward the south.

00:19:26.531 --> 00:19:27.566
 [sigh]

00:19:56.928 --> 00:19:57.862
 Congratulations, man.

00:19:57.962 --> 00:19:58.730
 Thanks.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:07.172
 Paul, I want to say thank
you for your hard work.

00:20:07.239 --> 00:20:08.940
You have what it takes
to fight in this forge.

00:20:09.007 --> 00:20:11.109
But unfortunately, I'm going
to have to ask you to please

00:20:11.176 --> 00:20:12.310
step off the forge floor.

00:20:12.377 --> 00:20:13.978
 Thank you, gentlemen.

00:20:14.045 --> 00:20:16.782
This was such a good experience
and it was an honor to compete

00:20:16.848 --> 00:20:18.283
against such a good competitor.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:19.917
 Isaac, we asked
you to build General

00:20:19.984 --> 00:20:21.586
Grant's Donaldson sword.

00:20:21.653 --> 00:20:24.623
You performed phenomenally and
built us something that is not

00:20:24.689 --> 00:20:27.859
only functional, but absolutely
beautiful and stunning

00:20:27.926 --> 00:20:28.993
to look at.

00:20:29.094 --> 00:20:31.396
You are the Forged
in Fire champion

00:20:31.463 --> 00:20:33.898
and you just earned yourself
a check for $10,000.

00:20:33.999 --> 00:20:35.233
Congratulations.

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:37.469
 I'm the Forged in
Fire champion, baby.

00:20:37.569 --> 00:20:39.605
Woo!

00:20:39.671 --> 00:20:41.138
 How do you feel?

00:20:41.205 --> 00:20:41.974
 Cloud nine.

00:20:42.074 --> 00:20:43.341
I'm feeling so good.

00:20:43.408 --> 00:20:45.176
 That's a remarkable
piece of work

00:20:45.243 --> 00:20:47.044
and you should be
incredibly proud of it.

00:20:47.111 --> 00:20:48.279
 Thank you.

00:20:48.346 --> 00:20:49.647
 There's just too
many feelings going

00:20:49.714 --> 00:20:53.117
through my head and my
heart to really process

00:20:53.217 --> 00:20:55.253
what's all happening right now.

00:20:55.353 --> 00:20:56.187
I can't believe it.

00:20:56.254 --> 00:20:57.656
I'm feeling so good.

00:21:06.464 --> 00:21:11.703
 The M1832 foot
artillery sword.

00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:13.838
NARRATOR: The M1832
foot artillery sword

00:21:13.939 --> 00:21:16.508
is the American recreation
of a French artillery

00:21:16.575 --> 00:21:20.044
sword modeled after the
infamous Roman gladius.

00:21:20.145 --> 00:21:21.546
Featuring a short
and stout blade,

00:21:21.612 --> 00:21:25.450
the weapon has an ornate
handle cast entirely of brass.

00:21:25.550 --> 00:21:27.085
Feathers or scales
are traditionally

00:21:27.152 --> 00:21:30.254
molded into the handle and an
eagle is etched into the palm

00:21:30.321 --> 00:21:31.856
well to honor America.

00:21:31.923 --> 00:21:33.992
Produced at the end
of the 19th century,

00:21:34.059 --> 00:21:36.894
the M1832 was issued
to artilleryman,

00:21:36.961 --> 00:21:40.064
but more widely used to clear
paths through thick brush

00:21:40.165 --> 00:21:42.934
and as the last
minute life saver.

00:21:43.034 --> 00:21:46.071
When called upon, the sword
was lethal in close quarters

00:21:46.171 --> 00:21:48.072
and was employed by
disemboweling horses

00:21:48.173 --> 00:21:49.473
to bring down the
rider, who then

00:21:49.573 --> 00:21:51.743
was finished in quick fashion.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:53.945
 To find out what
kind of deadly force

00:21:54.046 --> 00:21:55.580
your artillery
swords can supply,

00:21:55.647 --> 00:21:57.783
I will take your weapon,
deliver killing slashes

00:21:57.883 --> 00:21:59.417
on this ballistics dummy.

00:21:59.484 --> 00:22:00.885
John, you're up first.
You're ready for this?

00:22:00.952 --> 00:22:01.787
 Ready.

00:22:26.411 --> 00:22:28.914
 All right, John, first
up, I like the beauty

00:22:28.980 --> 00:22:30.282
of an all metal construction.

00:22:30.349 --> 00:22:32.851
And the Damascus fashion
you have here is gorgeous.

00:22:32.951 --> 00:22:34.819
The weight is all the
way in the handle allows

00:22:34.919 --> 00:22:38.389
for a good recovery and
forward delivery of strikes.

00:22:38.456 --> 00:22:40.559
Your edges are very sharp.

00:22:40.625 --> 00:22:43.828
Every cut cuts deep, cuts to
the bone, and into the organs.

00:22:43.895 --> 00:22:46.864
And most importantly,
sir, it will kill.

00:22:46.964 --> 00:22:48.233
 Thank you.

00:22:48.333 --> 00:22:49.900
 All right, Tom, your turn.
You ready?

00:22:50.001 --> 00:22:50.769
 Get her done.

00:23:11.556 --> 00:23:13.658
 All right, Tommy, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:23:13.759 --> 00:23:14.825
It is a beast.

00:23:14.892 --> 00:23:17.495
The weight of your
weapon is all forward

00:23:17.562 --> 00:23:19.463
that it actually
takes a lot to pull

00:23:19.530 --> 00:23:21.500
it away for a second strike.

00:23:21.600 --> 00:23:24.969
But the thing that your beaste
does have is a very sharp edge.

00:23:25.036 --> 00:23:26.971
Every cut is very deep.

00:23:27.072 --> 00:23:29.707
But it takes a lot of work
to control this beast.

00:23:29.774 --> 00:23:32.611
More importantly though,
sir, it will kill.

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:38.249
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:23:38.316 --> 00:23:40.051
Now why bring swords
to a gun range?

00:23:40.151 --> 00:23:43.588
Well, so you two can join one
of our two clubs, the oh my god,

00:23:43.688 --> 00:23:46.023
they broke my blade
with a bullet club,

00:23:46.123 --> 00:23:48.226
or the bulletproof sword club.

00:23:48.293 --> 00:23:49.460
So to test your
blades, we've got

00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:51.028
our firearm locked in a vise.

00:23:51.095 --> 00:23:52.931
We've got your blade locked
in another vise down range.

00:23:52.997 --> 00:23:55.066
We're going to fire one
round at that thing.

00:23:55.133 --> 00:23:58.135
It should split that bullet
clean or, worst of all,

00:23:58.202 --> 00:23:59.838
see that blade shatter.

00:23:59.938 --> 00:24:00.539
John, you're up first.

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:01.239
You ready for this?

00:24:01.339 --> 00:24:01.973
 Yeah.

00:24:02.073 --> 00:24:05.444
 OK, Fire.

00:24:08.446 --> 00:24:09.214
 Four holes.

00:24:19.657 --> 00:24:22.393
 I thought I felt that
you lost a hair of edge.

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.362
That's bullet hung
up on the blade.

00:24:24.429 --> 00:24:25.430
 Awesome.

00:24:25.497 --> 00:24:26.831
 You're going to
actually see top

00:24:26.898 --> 00:24:29.634
and bottom where that bullet
went across your blade.

00:24:29.701 --> 00:24:31.536
You can see there's four
holes in thing over there.

00:24:31.603 --> 00:24:33.070
That's the lead
core and the jacket

00:24:33.170 --> 00:24:34.605
going in different directions.

00:24:34.705 --> 00:24:36.240
So you split that bullet nicely.

00:24:36.340 --> 00:24:38.743
I don't see any
damage to your blade.

00:24:38.843 --> 00:24:39.411
Well done.

00:24:39.511 --> 00:24:40.144
Good job.

00:24:40.211 --> 00:24:41.379
 Thank you.

00:24:41.479 --> 00:24:42.547
 All right, Tommy,
are you ready for this?

00:24:42.647 --> 00:24:43.615
NARRATOR: Let's do it.

00:24:43.715 --> 00:24:44.483
 Fire.

00:24:47.351 --> 00:24:48.153
 Here we go.

00:24:53.925 --> 00:24:56.461
 All right, Tommy, well,
your blade took some damage

00:24:56.561 --> 00:24:57.561
in that bullet test.

00:24:57.628 --> 00:24:59.130
There's a chip in one spot.

00:24:59.230 --> 00:25:02.166
And the other spot, you can
actually hear my fingernail

00:25:02.233 --> 00:25:03.568
catching on that roll.

00:25:03.635 --> 00:25:06.437
Having said that, it
doesn't feel bad in my hand.

00:25:06.537 --> 00:25:08.607
But it is very heavy
for this type of sword.

00:25:08.707 --> 00:25:12.043
But as far as the strength test
goes, as you can clearly see,

00:25:12.110 --> 00:25:13.044
it took some damage.

00:25:15.947 --> 00:25:17.582
 All right,
bladesmiths, now that we

00:25:17.649 --> 00:25:19.384
know your blades
can take a bullet,

00:25:19.484 --> 00:25:20.852
it's time to find
out if they can cut.

00:25:20.919 --> 00:25:25.456
This is the sharpness
test, the shot bag slice.

00:25:25.523 --> 00:25:27.091
Now unlike the
strength test, this

00:25:27.158 --> 00:25:29.060
is all about what the
edge of your blade

00:25:29.127 --> 00:25:30.595
will do to these shot bags.

00:25:30.662 --> 00:25:32.897
A sharp blade
should cut cleanly.

00:25:32.963 --> 00:25:34.365
John, you're up first.
You ready for this?

00:25:34.465 --> 00:25:35.767
- Yeah.
- Let's do this.

00:25:52.284 --> 00:25:53.751
 Good job, man.

00:25:53.818 --> 00:25:56.288
 This is what I love about
your blade, the balance.

00:25:56.388 --> 00:25:57.555
It is fun to wield.

00:25:57.655 --> 00:25:59.190
It is fun to move around.

00:25:59.257 --> 00:26:01.492
It cuts with every slice.

00:26:01.559 --> 00:26:02.960
It will cut.

00:26:03.027 --> 00:26:03.995
 Thank you.

00:26:04.062 --> 00:26:05.296
 All right, Tommy,
it's your turn, sir.

00:26:05.363 --> 00:26:06.698
Are you ready?
- Let's do it.

00:26:20.879 --> 00:26:21.946
 Awesome.

00:26:22.012 --> 00:26:23.648
 All right, Tommy, on
the stationary cuts,

00:26:23.715 --> 00:26:24.649
it cuts cleanly.

00:26:24.716 --> 00:26:26.016
It's a sharp blade.

00:26:26.117 --> 00:26:28.353
Now when I'm moving around
and changing my balance,

00:26:28.453 --> 00:26:31.121
because of the weight of the
blade it does affect the way

00:26:31.188 --> 00:26:32.591
I'm cutting.

00:26:32.691 --> 00:26:34.291
So some of the cuts are not
clean all the way through.

00:26:34.358 --> 00:26:35.460
There are some strands.

00:26:35.526 --> 00:26:36.861
More importantly,
your weapon here,

00:26:36.961 --> 00:26:41.332
though, a beast, it will cut.

00:26:41.399 --> 00:26:44.502
 John, Tommy, the judges have
made their final decision.

00:26:44.602 --> 00:26:50.541
Our new Forged in
Fire champion is John.

00:26:50.608 --> 00:26:51.743
Congratulations.

00:26:51.809 --> 00:26:53.144
You're the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:26:53.210 --> 00:26:56.647
Tommy, unfortunately, your
blade didn't make the cut.

00:26:56.747 --> 00:26:58.149
 Tommy, this came
down to three things.

00:26:58.216 --> 00:27:00.919
The weight of your blade
made it harder to wield.

00:27:00.986 --> 00:27:03.121
Its rough construction
and the fact that it took

00:27:03.221 --> 00:27:04.456
damage in the strength test.

00:27:04.522 --> 00:27:07.759
Those are the reason
we're letting you go.

00:27:07.859 --> 00:27:09.093
 Tommy, you made a beast.

00:27:09.160 --> 00:27:11.162
But today, it
didn't make the cut.

00:27:11.262 --> 00:27:13.497
Please leave the range.

00:27:13.564 --> 00:27:14.699
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

00:27:14.766 --> 00:27:15.900
 From here, it's
just about getting

00:27:16.000 --> 00:27:17.435
better and refining my skills.

00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:18.836
 John, congratulations.

00:27:18.936 --> 00:27:20.738
You are the Forged
in Fire champion.

00:27:20.838 --> 00:27:24.241
And that is a title that comes
with a check for $10,000.

00:27:24.341 --> 00:27:25.142
Good job, brother.

00:27:25.209 --> 00:27:26.444
 Thank you.

00:27:26.544 --> 00:27:28.613
 It feels great to be the
next Forged in Fire champion.

00:27:28.680 --> 00:27:30.815
I'm super proud of all
the work that I've done.

00:27:30.882 --> 00:27:33.684
I've come here and
done tasks that I never

00:27:33.785 --> 00:27:36.388
would have expected from
myself and the challenges

00:27:36.454 --> 00:27:38.356
that I never would
have tried before.

00:27:38.456 --> 00:27:40.391
And I've succeeded.

00:27:40.491 --> 00:27:41.993
So I feel awesome.

00:27:49.933 --> 00:27:53.037
 The Springfield 905 bayonet.

00:27:53.104 --> 00:27:55.273
We will be providing
a Springfield

00:27:55.373 --> 00:27:58.409
1903 replica rifle to you.

00:27:58.475 --> 00:28:04.348
Your bayonets must fit snugly
and securely on your rifle.

00:28:04.448 --> 00:28:06.451
 [bleep]

00:28:06.551 --> 00:28:08.386
NARRATOR: Developed
in the early 1900s,

00:28:08.453 --> 00:28:10.988
the m1905 Springfield
bayonet was

00:28:11.055 --> 00:28:14.092
used by American infantry
for nearly 70 years

00:28:14.158 --> 00:28:16.561
from World War I
through the Vietnam War.

00:28:16.627 --> 00:28:18.196
These versatile
weapons were designed

00:28:18.263 --> 00:28:20.832
with a mechanical device in the
pommel that attached securely

00:28:20.898 --> 00:28:23.935
to the rifle while also
featuring a comfortable handle,

00:28:24.035 --> 00:28:26.938
making it a very effective
weapon in hand-to-hand combat.

00:28:27.038 --> 00:28:30.908
Featuring a sharp single edge,
a long fuller, and a false edge,

00:28:31.008 --> 00:28:33.777
this lightweight bayonet
could quickly deliver stabs

00:28:33.844 --> 00:28:35.780
and slashes to an opponent.

00:28:35.847 --> 00:28:38.916
The bayonet is still used today
during military ceremonies

00:28:38.983 --> 00:28:42.687
and can be seen in several
classic war films like 1998's

00:28:42.787 --> 00:28:43.888
"The Thin Red Line".

00:28:43.988 --> 00:28:46.958
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the kill test.

00:28:47.058 --> 00:28:49.760
The first mission today
is to take your bayonet

00:28:49.861 --> 00:28:51.362
and affix it to
Springfield rifle

00:28:51.462 --> 00:28:54.799
and deliver some killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:28:54.866 --> 00:28:57.902
Then I will dismantle
the blade from the rifle.

00:28:58.002 --> 00:28:59.403
And let's see what
kind of lethal damage

00:28:59.503 --> 00:29:00.571
it will do on its own.

00:29:00.638 --> 00:29:01.306
Josh, you're up first.

00:29:01.406 --> 00:29:02.273
You ready?

00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:03.141
 As ready as I can be.

00:29:26.530 --> 00:29:27.865
That's pretty badass.

00:29:27.965 --> 00:29:29.567
 All right, Josh, let's
talk about your bayonet here.

00:29:29.667 --> 00:29:31.702
When I affixed this
on to the rifle,

00:29:31.769 --> 00:29:34.705
it had a very nice
match with the railing

00:29:34.772 --> 00:29:35.840
in there and your pin.

00:29:35.907 --> 00:29:36.940
It was very secure.

00:29:37.007 --> 00:29:39.744
Now your edge is very sharp.

00:29:39.844 --> 00:29:43.114
It's definitely lacerates
deep into the bone.

00:29:43.214 --> 00:29:45.516
On its own, the
handle construction

00:29:45.616 --> 00:29:48.452
matches nicely on my hand.

00:29:48.519 --> 00:29:51.322
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:29:51.389 --> 00:29:52.323
 Awesome, thank you.

00:29:52.390 --> 00:29:53.391
 All right, Brad, your turn.

00:29:53.491 --> 00:29:54.391
So are you ready for this?

00:29:54.491 --> 00:29:55.193
 Let's go for it.

00:30:12.109 --> 00:30:14.946
 All right, Brad, first
up, the handle construction.

00:30:15.046 --> 00:30:17.048
It is a little bit
on the smaller side.

00:30:17.114 --> 00:30:18.816
But there are no sharp edges.

00:30:18.882 --> 00:30:20.050
And the flair you
have here actually

00:30:20.117 --> 00:30:21.652
gives me good
attention and I can

00:30:21.718 --> 00:30:23.120
get all the way to the guard.

00:30:23.187 --> 00:30:25.123
At first, I was a little bit
worried about your cutter

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:26.223
pin right here.

00:30:26.290 --> 00:30:28.592
It looked flimsy, but
the minute I put it on,

00:30:28.659 --> 00:30:29.927
it wasn't an issue at all.

00:30:29.994 --> 00:30:32.230
It stayed affixed to the
bayonet quite tightly.

00:30:32.330 --> 00:30:33.898
Your weapon is straight.

00:30:33.965 --> 00:30:37.569
Every cut was very deep
into this ballistics dummy.

00:30:37.635 --> 00:30:39.904
Overall sir, your
weapon will kill.

00:30:39.971 --> 00:30:40.905
 Thank you, sir.

00:30:44.008 --> 00:30:45.976
 Bladesmiths, welcome to
the strength test, the steel

00:30:46.076 --> 00:30:48.780
can, stab, and barricade chop.

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:51.048
This test is all about what
happens to your bayonets

00:30:51.148 --> 00:30:52.516
and not what happens
to the targets.

00:30:52.583 --> 00:30:53.350
Josh, you're up first.

00:30:53.417 --> 00:30:54.085
You ready?

00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:56.487
 No.

00:30:56.554 --> 00:31:04.395
[bleep] Here's my finish.

00:31:13.437 --> 00:31:16.039
 All right, Josh, well,
it survived really well.

00:31:16.140 --> 00:31:18.709
There is sections
on here that are

00:31:18.775 --> 00:31:20.077
now not as sharp as they were.

00:31:20.144 --> 00:31:21.545
But nothing rolled over.

00:31:21.612 --> 00:31:22.680
Nothing chipped out.

00:31:22.780 --> 00:31:24.515
Your point is still
nice and sharp.

00:31:24.582 --> 00:31:26.317
It performed really well
on the strength test.

00:31:26.417 --> 00:31:27.318
Nice job.
- Awesome.

00:31:27.418 --> 00:31:28.386
Thank you.

00:31:28.452 --> 00:31:29.820
 All right, Brad, are
you ready for this?

00:31:29.887 --> 00:31:30.687
 Well, my nan said,
don't break it.

00:31:30.788 --> 00:31:31.556
But go for it.

00:31:47.005 --> 00:31:50.275
 Well, Brad, what you
got here, your blade edge

00:31:50.341 --> 00:31:51.475
took some damage.

00:31:51.576 --> 00:31:54.111
The blade's taken a bit of
a bend to one side here.

00:31:54.178 --> 00:31:55.313
It's cheating to the right.

00:31:55.379 --> 00:31:57.481
But your point didn't
take any damage.

00:31:57.548 --> 00:31:58.516
It's all in one piece.

00:31:58.616 --> 00:31:59.550
It's a nice, sturdy blade.

00:31:59.617 --> 00:32:00.317
Nice job.

00:32:00.384 --> 00:32:01.152
 Thank you.

00:32:04.388 --> 00:32:06.557
 All right, bladesmiths,
this is the sharpness

00:32:06.657 --> 00:32:08.693
test, the military bag slice.

00:32:08.793 --> 00:32:12.062
To find out how sharp your edges
and point of your bayonets are,

00:32:12.129 --> 00:32:14.831
I'm going to take a stab
at these military bags.

00:32:14.932 --> 00:32:16.267
Josh, you're up first.
You ready?

00:32:16.367 --> 00:32:17.135
 Let's go for it.

00:32:31.415 --> 00:32:33.717
 All right, Josh,
you're bayonet right here

00:32:33.784 --> 00:32:38.455
had no problems puncturing the
bag and slicing it to pieces.

00:32:38.522 --> 00:32:39.356
It'll cut.

00:32:39.456 --> 00:32:40.124
 Sweet.

00:32:40.191 --> 00:32:41.292
Thanks.

00:32:41.359 --> 00:32:42.760
 All right, Brad,
your turn, sir.

00:32:42.827 --> 00:32:43.660
Shall we do it?

00:32:43.727 --> 00:32:45.363
 Of course, have at you.

00:33:01.545 --> 00:33:03.581
 All right, Brad, let's
talk about your blade

00:33:03.681 --> 00:33:05.282
here, wicked sharp.

00:33:05.382 --> 00:33:07.618
It punctured easily
in the military bag.

00:33:07.684 --> 00:33:12.289
At the same time, the edges
cut like hot steel on butter.

00:33:12.389 --> 00:33:16.060
Overall, sir, for this
test, it will cut.

00:33:16.127 --> 00:33:17.594
 Thank you, sir.

00:33:17.661 --> 00:33:20.063
 While you both brought us
amazing work, only one of you

00:33:20.130 --> 00:33:21.899
go home with the title.

00:33:21.966 --> 00:33:29.373
And the Forged in
Fire champion is Josh.

00:33:29.473 --> 00:33:30.041
 Holy shit.

00:33:30.107 --> 00:33:31.608
 Congratulations.

00:33:31.675 --> 00:33:33.411
 Brad, unfortunately, you're
not going home with the win

00:33:33.477 --> 00:33:35.179
today and Doug's
going to tell you why.

00:33:35.279 --> 00:33:36.514
 I commend you on your work.

00:33:36.580 --> 00:33:38.449
Your knife performed
very well on our test.

00:33:38.549 --> 00:33:40.083
But it was also the
only knife that took

00:33:40.150 --> 00:33:41.585
a band on the strength test.

00:33:41.652 --> 00:33:44.221
And for that reason, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:33:44.288 --> 00:33:45.623
 Brad, unfortunately,
that means

00:33:45.723 --> 00:33:47.091
we have to ask you to please
leave the forge floor.

00:33:47.158 --> 00:33:48.091
 I understand.

00:33:48.158 --> 00:33:48.959
Have a good one, guys.

00:33:49.060 --> 00:33:49.660
 Pleasure, man.

00:33:49.760 --> 00:33:51.228
 Thank you.

00:33:51.328 --> 00:33:52.630
 Well, Josh, that means you
are the Forged in Fire champion

00:33:52.697 --> 00:33:55.400
and you're going home
with a check for $10,000.

00:33:55.466 --> 00:33:56.334
How does it feel?

00:33:56.401 --> 00:33:57.368
 I feel awesome.

00:33:57.468 --> 00:33:58.703
 Congratulations.

00:34:01.205 --> 00:34:02.973
 I don't even know, man.

00:34:03.040 --> 00:34:05.609
I'm still trying to
sink in that I won.

00:34:05.676 --> 00:34:07.144
A little overwhelming.

00:34:07.210 --> 00:34:08.612
I can't wait to tell my wife.

00:34:08.679 --> 00:34:10.448
She had a lot of confidence
in me from the very start.

00:34:10.515 --> 00:34:13.483
I'm excited to let her know
that, hey, you were right.

00:34:13.550 --> 00:34:15.319
I won.

